# SPRAWL

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Sprawl is a combat-specific defensive movement designed to rapidly project the hips backward while lowering the center of mass to defend against takedowns and immediately regain an effective fighting position.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer combat movement exercises for developing explosive defensive reactions, whole-body coordination and repeated power output.

---

# Philosophy

A successful sprawl is not simply a defensive technique.

It is an explosive athletic action requiring reaction speed, coordination, hip power, trunk stiffness and rapid recovery.

CAS selects the Sprawl whenever the athlete must improve takedown defense, reactive explosiveness or combat-specific conditioning.

